### `plan.md`

```markdown
# Technical Implementation Plan: UserSettingsView Material 3 Refactor

## 1. Architectural Overview
We will refactor the styling of `UserSettingsView` by introducing a centralized Material 3 design token system using CSS Custom Properties (variables). This ensures that theme switching is handled natively by the browser without requiring a complete re-render of the DOM.

```
[Global Styles / Theme Provider]
       │
       ├──> _tokens.scss (Defines M3 CSS variables for Light/Dark)
       │
[UserSettingsView Component]
       │
       └──> user-settings-view.scss (Consumes CSS variables, defines layout)
```

## 2. Design Token Architecture
We will create a dedicated SCSS partial `_tokens.scss` that defines the Material 3 design tokens.

### 2.1. Light Theme (Default)
Mapped to `:root` or a default state:
```css
:root {
  /* Colors - Light Palette (Brand Tone 40 for Primary) */
  --md-sys-color-primary: #0061a4; /* Accessible brand blue */
  --md-sys-color-on-primary: #ffffff;
  --md-sys-color-primary-container: #d1e4ff;
  --md-sys-color-on-primary-container: #001d36;

  --md-sys-color-surface: #fdfcff;
  --md-sys-color-on-surface: #1a1c1e;
  --md-sys-color-surface-variant: #dfe2eb;
  --md-sys-color-on-surface-variant: #43474e;
  --md-sys-color-outline: #73777f;
  --md-sys-color-background: #fdfcff;
  --md-sys-color-on-background: #1a1c1e;

  /* Typography Scale */
  --md-sys-typescale-headline-medium: 500 1.75rem/2.25rem 'Roboto', sans-serif;
  --md-sys-typescale-body-large: 400 1rem/1.5rem 'Roboto', sans-serif;
  --md-sys-typescale-label-large: 500 0.875rem/1.25rem 'Roboto', sans-serif;

  /* Shapes */
  --md-sys-shape-corner-none: 0px;
  --md-sys-shape-corner-small: 4px;
  --md-sys-shape-corner-medium: 8px;
  --md-sys-shape-corner-large: 16px;

  /* Spacing */
  --md-sys-spacing-xs: 4px;
  --md-sys-spacing-sm: 8px;
  --md-sys-spacing-md: 16px;
  --md-sys-spacing-lg: 24px;
  --md-sys-spacing-xl: 32px;
}
```

### 2.2. Dark Theme (Fallback High-Luminance Tokens)
Mapped to `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` and the override selector `[data-theme="dark"]`:
```css
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root {
    /* Colors - Dark Palette (Brand Tone 80 for Primary to ensure 4.5:1 contrast) */
    --md-sys-color-primary: #9ecaff; /* High-luminance fallback brand blue */
    --md-sys-color-on-primary: #003258;
    --md-sys-color-primary-container: #00497d;
    --md-sys-color-on-primary-container: #d1e4ff;

    --md-sys-color-surface: #1a1c1e;
    --md-sys-color-on-surface: #e2e2e6;
    --md-sys-color-surface-variant: #43474e;
    --md-sys-color-on-surface-variant: #c3c7d0;
    --md-sys-color-outline: #8d9199;
    --md-sys-color-background: #1a1c1e;
    --md-sys-color-on-background: #e2e2e6;
  }
}

/* Manual override selector */
[data-theme="dark"] {
  --md-sys-color-primary: #9ecaff;
  --md-sys-color-on-primary: #003258;
  --md-sys-color-primary-container: #00497d;
  --md-sys-color-on-primary-container: #d1e4ff;

  --md-sys-color-surface: #1a1c1e;
  --md-sys-color-on-surface: #e2e2e6;
  --md-sys-color-surface-variant: #43474e;
  --md-sys-color-on-surface-variant: #c3c7d0;
  --md-sys-color-outline: #8d9199;
  --md-sys-color-background: #1a1c1e;
  --md-sys-color-on-background: #e2e2e6;
}
```

## 3. Theme Detection & Switching Utility
We will implement a lightweight, framework-agnostic TypeScript utility `ThemeManager` to handle manual overrides and system preference listening.

### API Interface:
```typescript
export class ThemeManager {
  static init(): void;
  static setTheme(theme: 'light' | 'dark' | 'system'): void;
  static getTheme(): 'light' | 'dark' | 'system';
  static getActiveTheme(): 'light' | 'dark';
}
```

## 4. Component SCSS Refactoring
The existing `user-settings-view.scss` will be refactored to:
1. Use `@use 'tokens'` to import design tokens.
2. Replace all hardcoded colors, margins, paddings, and border-radii with M3 CSS variables.
3. Implement a responsive flex/grid layout:
   - Mobile (< 600px): Single column, full-width form fields.
   - Tablet/Desktop (>= 600px): Two-column layout (navigation/categories on the left, settings form on the right).

## 5. Testing Strategy
- **Unit Tests:**
  - `ThemeManager` unit tests must cover all branches (system preference changes, manual overrides, local storage persistence) with **>85% branch coverage**.
- **Contrast Verification:**
  - Programmatic or manual verification of WCAG AA compliance (4.5:1 contrast ratio) for all text elements in both light and dark modes.
- **Regression Testing:**
  - Verify that all form submission, validation, and API interaction logic remains completely untouched and fully functional.
```

