### Solution Architect Analysis & Resolution

This is a classic Material 3 architectural challenge. In dark themes, directly using a brand’s core saturated/dark color (e.g., `Primary40` `#6750A4`) against dark surfaces (`#141218`) results in a contrast ratio of **~2.1:1**, which severely violates WCAG 2.1 AA (4.5:1 minimum).

Material 3 solves this via **HCT (Hue, Chroma, Tone) Tonal Palettes** and paired **"On-Color" / "Container" token roles**.

---

### 1. Solution Architect (SA) Strategy: Tonal Palette Derivation

Instead of reusing the exact brand hex code in dark mode, M3 extracts the source brand hue and shifts the **Luminance Tone**:

```
Source Brand Color (#6750A4, Tone 40)
       │
       ├──► Light Theme Surface (#FEF7FF, Tone 98)
       │      └─► Consumes Primary40 (#6750A4)  ──► Contrast Ratio: 7.2:1 ✅
       │
       └──► Dark Theme Surface (#141218, Tone 6)
              ├─► Standalone text/icons consume Primary80 (#D0BCFF) ──► Contrast Ratio: 9.6:1 ✅
              └─► Filled Brand Buttons consume:
                    ├─ Background: Primary80 (#D0BCFF, Tone 80)
                    └─ Foreground text: On-Primary20 (#381E72, Tone 20) ──► Contrast Ratio: 7.8:1 ✅
```

#### Token Definitions & Mathematical Contrast Ratios

| Token Role | Light Mode Value | Light Contrast vs Surface (`#FEF7FF`) | Dark Mode Value | Dark Contrast vs Surface (`#141218`) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `--md-sys-color-primary` | `#6750A4` (Tone 40) | **7.2 : 1** (Passes AA/AAA) | `#D0BCFF` (Tone 80) | **9.6 : 1** (Passes AA/AAA) |
| `--md-sys-color-on-primary` | `#FFFFFF` (Tone 100)| **4.8 : 1** (on `#6750A4`) | `#381E72` (Tone 20) | **7.8 : 1** (on `#D0BCFF`) |
| `--md-sys-color-primary-container` | `#EADDFF` (Tone 90) | — | `#4F378B` (Tone 30) | — |
| `--md-sys-color-on-primary-container` | `#21005D` (Tone 10) | **11.2 : 1** (on Container) | `#EADDFF` (Tone 90) | **8.1 : 1** (on Container) |

---

